  "limitations": [
    "One fresh direct Telnet process executes the immutable dual-axis-retention schedule 91x20 -> 61x14 (one window request changing both axes) -> 91x20; every stage is observed before the next resize.",
    "After the dual-axis shrink, one fixed CUP(7;2)+\"DQ\" write and DSR are sent; after the dual restore, DSR only. No other CUP, CR/LF, redraw or replacement text is sent.",
    "Stage zero requires every preloaded sentinel and DSR19;7; later missing markers and the observed write position are observations, never semantic acceptance.",
    "The dual-axis 61x14 endpoint and its NAWS event count/order are saved before assertions; the request is one window action, not an assumed atomic two-axis transport event. No calibration or retries.",
    "The one write is recorded through its document line, text offset and DSR; no general original position-unit, scroll or C++ Cell mapping is inferred.",
    "The existing geometry and sequential width/height records identify prior evidence only; this run does not inherit their semantic behavior.",
    "DSR safety bounds remain row1..200/column1..500 independently of the fourteen-row viewport.",
    "Only finite ASCII source-derived catalog strings may be published, with complete reconstructible document arrays. Unrestricted recording stays private.",
    "This single schedule does not establish alternate-frame, Unicode, arbitrary dimensions or resize order, further post-resize editing, ConPTY, performance or R2 acceptance, and does not merge the original observation with any confirmed TermForge difference."
  ]
